    "summary": "I built a cabinet three storeys high with three drawers, one on each level. It's a stack of three north-half hex bases at cell (0,0), levels 0–2, held together by the snaps added automatically between levels. Each storey has a drawer fitted on the cut face of its half base. I ran the house rules, capping the open faces with 6 end caps and bolting the joints. The configurator check passed with no rule issues, and the collision check came back clear. The build has 31 parts and the estimate is about 1820 g of filament and 2633 minutes of printing. I didn't add any props, since the brief only asked for the cabinet itself.",
